WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.063
Hello, I'm Gav.

00:00:01.063 --> 00:00:01.896
I'm Dan.

00:00:01.896 --> 00:00:02.730
We are The Slow Mo Guys and today,

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.300
we're not in my back garden
where it's nice and bright.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.120
We're in my dark, dingy garage
where we keep our props.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.400
It's unusual for us.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.420
The reason for that is because
we've had a lot of requests

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.450
to film an iris constricting when it comes

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.090
into a lot of light very suddenly.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:17.070
You can't do that outside.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.650
And we're gonna film this on a macro lens

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:19.760
a thousand frames a second.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.470
Usually, the macro lenses we've used,

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:24.040
they're slightly bulky and
I think I actually struggled

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.760
to get at your eyeball because
of your big old eyebrow.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:28.830
My Neanderthal brow.

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.340
And eye socket.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.400
So we're using this Laowa macro lens,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.510
which is a very odd
shape, but after we take

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.410
the lens cap off, it also has LED lighting

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:40.670
and I think with this,
I'll actually be able

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:43.380
to get right up against your ball.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.213
My eyeball.

00:00:44.213 --> 00:00:45.046
Oh, God.

00:00:45.046 --> 00:00:46.320
As long as you don't poke my eye out.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:47.220
I'll try not to.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:51.370
The widest aperture on this lens is an F14

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.690
which is actually gonna make it very dark

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.530
when we're shooting at a
thousand frames a second,

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.090
so it's very good that it's
got a light on the end of it.

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:00.490
Stick it on the camera here.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.780
It's actually longer than the camera.

00:01:07.610 --> 00:01:08.840
Well we can either film your eye

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:12.115
or I can give you some sort
of medical examination.

00:01:12.115 --> 00:01:14.250
I know which one I'd prefer.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:18.280
So when sat close it looks
like just a normal lens

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.883
except we can go much, much closer.

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:32.300
Down a bit, to your eye. There you go.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.960
Down slightly. Perfect. You're
right in the middle of that.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.430
God, even just my breathing

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.540
is rocking me all over the place.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:40.680
Don't bash your eyeball.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:42.680
Oh, you can feel your eyelashes.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:45.530
I mean, honestly this is gonna be

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:47.850
one of the easier videos
for me technically to do

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:50.350
cause all I have to do is
sit in a chair really still.

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:51.940
But at the same time it's not relaxing

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:54.260
cause I'm gonna have this
huge lens shoved in my eyeball

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:56.220
and a bunch of bright lights
turned on immediately.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:57.053
Yeah.

00:01:57.997 --> 00:02:00.883
bloody hell. No big
movements anymore, okay?

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.150
Plug in the lense power.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:06.550
Oh my God that's bright.

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:09.493
The thing is, my heart
beat is moving my eye.

00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.490
I'm gonna turn it off,
gonna set the frame rate

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.160
back to a thousand

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.333
and I'm gonna turn the
lights off in here for a bit.

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:24.243
Oooh, that is dark.

00:02:24.243 --> 00:02:26.970
You know I got like floaties now.

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:28.353
You got floaties?

00:02:28.353 --> 00:02:31.130
Yeah. Don't make me laugh, I'll move.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:32.180
All right, you ready?

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:33.013
Yeah.

00:02:33.013 --> 00:02:35.000
Three, two, one

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.843
Ah, oh, that is mental.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.840
I got actually a donut in my eye now.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.793
All I can see is a huge
fat pink and blue donut.

00:02:49.884 --> 00:02:51.160
Turn the light on.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.960
Oh, it's completely blue now.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.390
I just got this blue ring in my vision.

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.493
Oh, it's really weird.

00:02:59.428 --> 00:03:00.730
Was it all right?

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:01.563
Look at it.

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:05.560
I don't think I've ever seen
an eye so open that close.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:10.003
Oh that's weird.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.673
The muscles haven't started moving yet.

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:20.810
Oh there they go. Now
it's closing. See that?

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:25.810
Yeah. God. Look at the
moisture on my eyeball.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.123
That is mental.

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.570
So the focus has changed slightly.

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:38.803
You decided you had enough.

00:03:40.204 --> 00:03:41.680
The thing is to me, I was like Ahhhh,

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:42.967
I want it gone.

00:03:44.687 --> 00:03:45.520
ooh gross.

00:03:51.855 --> 00:03:54.262
What's that right there? What is that?

00:03:54.262 --> 00:03:58.190
Oh it's so disgusting. That's madness.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:02.100
Maybe turn the light a little less bright?

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:03.830
I could do it less bright

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:05.630
and I can maybe half the frame rate.

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:07.903
To 500.

00:04:07.903 --> 00:04:09.340
Yeah, I think that might be a good idea.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:11.610
The thing is my heart beat is moving me.

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:15.160
And you making me laugh
is making me move a bunch.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:20.160
Oh this is amazing. We're
on the closest I can be.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:21.510
3, 2, 1

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:24.333
Oh. Phew

00:04:24.333 --> 00:04:26.163
Bloody good. Amazing.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.800
That was really good.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.320
So you're all right?

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:31.530
Flipping heck.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:33.730
Right, this is what's happening, okay.

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:38.730
First of all, that's
outrageous for a start.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:42.840
Then it's immediately just a
flash of just pure brightness

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.770
and then it slowly turns into a donut.

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:47.180
The donut is originally like this

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:49.640
and then it becomes a donut
with a bigger hole in the middle

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.371
because my eye is constricting

00:04:51.371 --> 00:04:53.510
and I can see more detail of the light

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:54.610
if you know what I mean.

00:05:06.069 --> 00:05:06.902
Ready?

00:05:06.902 --> 00:05:08.069
Mm hm.

00:05:10.571 --> 00:05:12.183
Oh.

00:05:12.183 --> 00:05:13.113
Wow. That looks so weird.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:18.683
It's starting to move.

00:05:18.683 --> 00:05:20.850
There's actually a small delay.

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:23.110
I wonder, we could probably
count that delay by the frames.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:24.533
And you see all these creases,

00:05:24.533 --> 00:05:27.670
they're actually really soft and fibrous.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:31.540
When your eye is completely
dilated they change shape.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:33.270
Oh, those holes on the outside of my eye

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.930
were so much fatter and
bigger, and now they're tall.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:36.763
Oval.

00:05:36.763 --> 00:05:37.910
Yeah.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:39.590
Isn't that weird. It
drags the entire pattern

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:41.330
and you an actually see the layers.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.260
But you can very clearly here

00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:46.420
see what is on top and what
is underneath of your iris.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:49.440
So weird. And my iris
isn't perfectly circular.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:51.310
See there's little bits on the outside

00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:53.380
that are coming around.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:54.300
It's true.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:57.010
It is crazy to think
that every single thing

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:59.933
you've ever seen was through that hole.

00:06:01.177 --> 00:06:02.558
Well, half of it.

00:06:02.558 --> 00:06:05.560
This is the closest to
the window to the soul

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:06.660
you can possibly be.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:08.840
You're basically trying
to look into my soul here.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.140
I reckon I can do this one thing

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:13.530
where I move my iris really
quickly from side to side.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:14.363
Oh, you shake your eyeball?

00:06:14.363 --> 00:06:16.650
Yeah, I shake my eyeball
slightly. Yeah, like that.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:17.570
Oh God.

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:18.693
You went cross-eyed.

00:06:19.940 --> 00:06:21.540
I can't do it quite as big as that

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:23.180
but I think cause we're so close

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.920
you should be able to
see a bit of shakage.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:26.000
And when I was filming my eye

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.510
and I was moving my eye
around, I could see,

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:31.160
because the iris is a
muscle and there's liquid,

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.020
it was jostling.

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:34.460
So I wonder if when your eye vibrates,

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.870
would it be sloshy almost.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:37.703
Weird.

00:06:37.703 --> 00:06:38.580
Yeah, we'll find out.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:41.740
That was it?

00:06:41.740 --> 00:06:42.573
Yeah.

00:06:42.573 --> 00:06:43.410
Oh, didn't know you did it.

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:44.710
Oh yeah, I was doing it.

00:06:51.295 --> 00:06:53.759
Oh, I'm salsa dancing my eye.

00:06:53.759 --> 00:06:56.102
I had no idea it was that liquidy.

00:06:56.102 --> 00:06:57.990
Oh my God. Do you see that?

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:01.253
So those areas of your
eye where there's craters,

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:02.973
they're loose.

00:07:02.973 --> 00:07:04.220
I didn't know that.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.750
They almost have their own
eyelids when you do that.

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.820
They do. Look how the
fibers are closing in

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.990
and moving about. Do you see that?

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.493
Looks like just like a
fat butt jiggling around.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:18.340
So gelatinous. It is like jelly.

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:21.650
It's almost like a weave,
like each one is a string.

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:22.900
I think that's what it is.

00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:24.650
That's the best way to describe it.

00:07:25.958 --> 00:07:26.924
It jiggles.

00:07:26.924 --> 00:07:28.210
It looks like spaghetti.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.430
Looks like overcooked
spaghetti moving around.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:33.790
Well that was some
graphic looking footage.

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:35.040
I might not be able to tell.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.480
How many fingers am I holding up?

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:37.640
One donut.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:38.473
That's about right.

00:07:38.473 --> 00:07:40.120
Yeah. God.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:41.144
I'll tell you what though,

00:07:41.144 --> 00:07:42.490
I don't think I can ever in the future

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:44.040
use iris recognition software

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:46.260
cause everyone has the
perfect image of my eyeball.

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:48.420
Yeah. An iris scan does not work.

00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:50.730
You got the least secure
iris now on the planet.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:53.200
And I've already filmed my
eye so we're both toast.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:54.670
Well, hopefully you enjoyed that video

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:56.450
or you were grossed out by it.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:59.390
I feel like either one
is a victory for us.

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:02.520
Please feel free to
subscribe to the Slo Mo Guys

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:05.600
and check back in a little
bit for the next video

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.900
when hopefully Dan will
be able to see again.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:08.990
Your life's in my hands now.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:11.153
I've gotta drive home with you in the

